  "instructions": [
    "Preheat woodfired grill to 120°C (250°F).",
    "In a small bowl, mix together woodfired BBQ sauce, Korean chili flakes, brown sugar, soy sauce, rice vinegar, garlic, and ginger.",
    "Place the beef ribs on the grill and brush the BBQ sauce mixture evenly over both sides of the ribs.",
    "Close the grill lid and cook for 2 hours, or until the ribs are tender and caramelized.",
    "During the last 10 minutes of cooking, brush the ribs with cherry jam and cook until caramelized.",
    "Remove the ribs from the grill and let rest for 10 minutes before serving.",
    "Serve with cherry chutney on the side."
